{"step_index":2448,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"CHECKPOINT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-27T12:23:18Z","content":"# Resuming from a compaction\n\nYou are continuing work on the task described above, but you have lost access to the full conversation history, and need to resume work efficiently using the progress summary below:\n\n# User Requests\nThe following were user requests from the truncated conversation in chronological order:\n1. ja push?\n2. Cara, nós vamos repaginar essa porra. Eu amei o parakeet ai. Vamos nos inspirar na IA, no formato operacional dele, tudo que for possivel. Consegue ver como ele é buildado? Ver as práticas de antiproctoring que ele usa, estudar a linguagem em que é escrito, o como ele opera, etc. Isso tudo antes de UI, que será o ultimo.  Eu tenho ele instalado C:\\Users\\Arthur Henrique\\AppData\\Local\\Programs\\parakeetai-desktop\n3. Resume\n4. Continue\n5. Sim, mas nao mude UI agora, apenas stack, a UI mudaremos depois. Apenas adequye pra o mesmo metodo deles, arquitetura e stack ser 1:1 com o nosso.\n6. como rodo?\n7. Com o parakeet aberto, fica assim: \n\nO nosso nao fica assim. e o .bat nunca deve aparecer o .bat atras, tipo, deve ser sempre apenas o electron (em .exe igual o parakeet)\n\nE outra coisa, como posso fazer pra os prints do Parakeet pegarem ele? Quero conseguir printar ele pra te mostrar a estrutura da UI/UX design dele, mas ele some em prints. (ESTOU com ele rodando nesse exato momento pra vc conseguir consultar e mimicar até mesmo o nome que ele poe no processo dele)\n8. Resume\n9. Adicione um botao de mover,. que ao clicar, vai aparecer esses 6 cambos na tela do user com esse overlay de opacidade e vai ser a forma do user definir onde o Spectra vai ficar, igual tem no parakeet e só vai mover por aí. \n10. Ok, agora vamos reformular o layout e UI do spectra. Ele deve ter a mesma interface do Parakeet, com a diferença que nao vai ter esse Buy Credits. DashBoard nao teremos por enquanto, mas deixe o botao lockado lá, tema deve ser branco igual o parakeet mas com a possibilidade de dar switch igual vemos que existe também nas settings do parakeet, private on ou off para poder printar, e o Create Session que traz os campos Sessin Type, Company e Job Description. NAO VAMOS COLOCAR pastte a job link, mas vamos ter esse campo CV / RESUME que nutrem o campo de conhecimento da ia (opcional mas bom) + Documentos (mesma coisa)\n\n<summary>\n### 1. Task Overview\n- **Goal**: Full overhaul of Spectra's UI/UX to match Parakeet AI 1:1 based on the user's provided screenshots (`media_1790511368271.png` and `media_1790511444466.png`).\n- **Core Requirements**:\n  1. Parakeet visual identity: Clean floating card (`border-radius: 24px`), soft shadow, default white theme, with a Light/Dark/System theme switcher in Settings.\n  2. Header: Logo (\"Spectra AI\"), Minimize (`⤢`), Move (`✥` - 6-slot positioning grid), Settings menu (`⋮`), Close (`✕`). No \"Buy Credits\" button.\n  3. Settings Dropdown: User account info, \"Check for Updates\", \"Dashboard\" (locked badge), \"Private\" switch with tooltip (toggles `SetWindowDisplayAffinity` on/off so user can take screenshots/prints), \"Meeting Detect\" (disabled), Zoom controls (`-`, `+`, `↺`), Theme switcher (`☀️`, `🌙`, `🌗`).\n  4. Main Hub / Dashboard View: Search bar with sort button, session card list (Date, Title, Subtitle, badges `[💼 Interview]` `[📝 Transcript]`, status `● Ended · 10m 0s · Free Session`, \"View Transcript\" button), and bottom bar with \"View in Dashboard\" (locked) and \"+ Create Session\" (vibrant green button).\n  5. Create Session Modal (Step 1 & Step 2):\n     - Left Stepper sidebar: \"Create Interview Session\", \"① Details\" (active), \"② Preferences\", and \"View Tutorial\" button.\n     - Form: Session Type (`Interview` vs `Regular` pill toggle), NO \"Paste a job link\" button, Company input, Job Description textarea, Context section with \"CV / Resume\" and \"Documents\" file/text inputs feeding the AI context.\n     - \"Cancel\" and \"Next\" buttons. Step 2 configures AI Provider, model, focus preset, and mic before launching live interview.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Progress\n- **Completed**:\n  - **Stack Migration**: Migrated from Python to Electron + Node.js 24 (`electron/main.js`, `electron/preload.js`, `electron/server/server.js`, `electron/server/session.js`, `electron/server/llm.js`, `electron/server/stt.js`, `electron/server/prompts.js`).\n  - **Process Camouflage**: Replicated Parakeet's Task Manager signature 1:1 (`\\u2800.exe` Braille blank space + `<title>pmodule</title>` in `web/index.html`).\n  - **Compiled Launchers**: Built Windows GUI launchers `Spectra.exe` and `⠀.exe` via C# (`launcher.cs`), eliminating console windows and `.bat` popups.\n  - **6-Slot Positioning Grid**: Created `web/move-overlay.html` and bound `Alt+M` / Move button (`✥`) to snap Spectra into 6 canonical screen zones.\n  - **1:1 Parakeet Stylesheet**: Created `web/css/parakeet-theme.css` covering Light and Dark themes, cards, stepper, pills, dropdowns, and live session stream.\n  - **UI Controller**: Created `web/js/parakeet-ui.js` handling theme switching, private mode IPC toggle, settings menu, Create Session stepper, resume/doc context upload, and session history persistence.\n  - **Main HTML Overhaul**: Replaced `web/index.html` with the Parakeet shell structure (Header, Hub, Stepper Modal, Live Session wrapper).\n  - **IPC Handlers**: Added `set-private-mode`, `get-private-mode`, `close-app`, `minimize-app`, `open-move-overlay`, and `select-location` to `electron/main.js` and `electron/preload.js`.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Key Findings & Decisions\n- **Process Camouflage Revelation**: Parakeet appears as `⠀ (6)` / `pmodule` in Task Manager because its executable is named `\\u2800.exe` (Unicode Braille Pattern Blank, hex 0x2800) and its HTML `<title>` is `pmodule`. We mirrored this in `web/index.html` and the compiled executables.\n- **Screenshot Invisibility**: Parakeet hides from screenshots via `mainWindow.setContentProtection(true)` (`SetWindowDisplayAffinity`). The \"Private\" switch in the dropdown menu directly toggles this flag to `false`, allowing standard Windows screenshots (`Win+Shift+S`).\n- **Parakeet 6-Slot Grid**: Extracted directly from module 76394 in Parakeet's `renderer.js` (`top-left`, `top-center`, `top-right`, `bottom-left`, `bottom-center`, `bottom-right`).\n- **No Subagents Constraint**: User explicitly commanded: *\"sem subagent pq isso estoura minha quota, faz voce um de cada vez\"*. Never spawn subagents.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Active Context\n- **Workspace**: `c:\\Users\\Arthur Henrique\\Documents\\GitHub\\Spectra`\n- **Key Files**:\n  - `web/index.html` (Parakeet UI layout)\n  - `web/css/parakeet-theme.css` (1:1 Parakeet styles & Light/Dark variables)\n  - `web/js/parakeet-ui.js` (UI state, stepper, theme, private mode, context management)\n  - `web/move-overlay.html` (6-slot overlay)\n  - `electron/main.js` (Window management, stealth protection, IPC handlers)\n  - `electron/preload.js` (Context bridge)\n  - `Spectra.exe` & `⠀.exe` (Native binary launchers)\n\n---\n\n### 5. Next Steps\n1. **Verify UI Execution**: Launch `Spectra.exe` (or `npm start`) and inspect the new layout live to confirm the visual styling matches the screenshots pixel-for-pixel in both Light and Dark modes.\n2. **End-to-End Session Creation Test**:\n   - Click `+ Create Session` -> Fill Company, Job Description, attach/verify Resume -> Click `Next` -> Verify Step 2 preferences -> Click `Start Session`.\n   - Verify that `onboardingData` (Resume + Job Description) is correctly ingested by `electron/server/session.js` and fed into the AI system prompts.\n3. **Validate Settings & Private Mode**: Test turning \"Private\" OFF in the settings dropdown and taking a test screenshot (`Win+Shift+S`) to confirm Spectra is visible, then turning it back ON to verify it disappears from capture.\n4. **Git Commit & Push**: Commit the new Parakeet UI and Electron integration to GitHub when verified.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Commitments & Constraints\n- **Do NOT use subagents** under any circumstances (user quota limit).\n- Maintain direct, informal Portuguese communication (\"Bora!\", \"viado\", \"cachorro\").\n- Keep \"Dashboard\" present in the UI but locked/disabled.\n- Omit \"Paste a job link\" from the Create Session modal.\n- Default theme is Light (white), with full Dark mode toggle capability.\n</summary>\n\nYou have the 10 following artifacts written to the artifacts directory:\n\n[ARTIFACT: agent]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/Arthur%20Henrique/.gemini/antigravity/brain/bbca0f09-2535-4f26-97c1-b43b75148a4f/.agents/agents/frontend-editor/agent.md\nLast Edited: 2026-08-21T22:23:41Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1787340675417]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/Arthur%20Henrique/.gemini/antigravity/brain/bbca0f09-2535-4f26-97c1-b43b75148a4f/.user_uploaded/media_1787340675417.png\nLast Edited: 2026-08-21T19:31:31Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1790485505932]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/Arthur%20Henrique/.gemini/antigravity/brain/bbca0f09-2535-4f26-97c1-b43b75148a4f/.user_uploaded/media_1790485505932.png\nLast Edited: 2026-09-27T05:05:38Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1790485882009]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/Arthur%20Henrique/.gemini/antigravity/brain/bbca0f09-2535-4f26-97c1-b43b75148a4f/.user_uploaded/media_1790485882009.png\nLast Edited: 2026-09-27T05:11:44Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1790486630185]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/Arthur%20Henrique/.gemini/antigravity/brain/bbca0f09-2535-4f26-97c1-b43b75148a4f/.user_uploaded/media_1790486630185.png\nLast Edited: 2026-09-27T05:24:52Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1790511368271]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/Arthur%20Henrique/.gemini/antigravity/brain/bbca0f09-2535-4f26-97c1-b43b75148a4f/.user_uploaded/media_1790511368271.png\nLast Edited: 2026-09-27T12:18:34Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1790511444466]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/Arthur%20Henrique/.gemini/antigravity/brain/bbca0f09-2535-4f26-97c1-b43b75148a4f/.user_uploaded/media_1790511444466.png\nLast Edited: 2026-09-27T12:18:34Z\n\n[A